..Title
Resolution to Approve Purchase of Servers, Software, and Professional Services from CDW Government, LLC for Computing Operations for the Water Resource Recovery Facility ($155,000.00)
..Memorandum
Attached for your review and approval is a resolution authorizing payment to CDW Government, LLC for new Dell servers utilizing the Nutanix Cloud Platform, including a Statement of Work outlining the professional services for implementation.

The Information Technology Department maintains local onsite servers at the Water Resource Recovery Facility to ensure business continuity and minimize the risk of operational disruptions. The proposed equipment purchase will replace aging hardware scheduled for decommissioning. This procurement utilizes the Sourcewell cooperative purchasing agreement to ensure competitive pricing.

Budget/Fiscal Impact: Total FY26 costs are $132,328.15.  A contingency of $22,671.85 is being requested to mitigate potential price fluctuations in the server hardware market due to the global shortage of high-capacity memory components and sustained demand from AI infrastructure. This expense was planned and budgeted for in the FY26 Information Technology Services Budget.
..Staff
Prepared by: Jennifer Grimes, Infrastructure and Cybersecurity Manager
Reviewed by: Joshua Baron, Director, Information Technology Services Unit
Approved by: Milton Dohoney, Jr., City Administrator
..Body
Whereas, Whereas, Dell servers provide key services to the City of Ann Arbor locally onsite at the Water Resource Recovery Facility;

Whereas, The purchase of three new servers will replace existing servers, which are aging and should be replaced for maximum reliability;

Whereas, The proposed purchase of servers, operating system, and professional services has been procured through the Sourcewell cooperative purchasing arrangement in accordance with City Code section 1:316(2);

Whereas, It is recommended that the City exercise its right to participate in such cooperative purchasing arrangement in accordance with the City Code; 

Whereas, The Information Technology Department has identified a requirement for a project contingency in the amount of $22,671.85 to mitigate potential price fluctuations in the server hardware market driven by global shortages of high-capacity memory components and sustained demand from AI infrastructure; and

Whereas, The City will be invoiced by CDW Government, LLC $132,328.15 and this amount has been budgeted in the FY26 Information Technology Services Budget;

RESOLVED, That City Council approve a purchase order with CDW Government, LLC for the acquisition of new servers, operating system, and professional services in FY26, pursuant to the attached quote and the Statement of Work, at a cost of $132,328.15;

RESOLVED, That City Council approve a contingency for this project in the amount of $22,671.85, subject to City Administrator approval;

RESOLVED, That the City Council finds that the Sourcewell cooperative purchasing arrangement is cost-effective and in the City's best interest;

RESOLVED, That the Mayor and City Clerk be authorized and directed to execute the Statement of Work, containing the professional services to be provided and the terms and conditions pertaining to those services ("Agreement"), after approval as to substance by the City Administrator and approval as to form by the City Attorney; and

RESOLVED, That the City Administrator be authorized to take all necessary actions to implement this Resolution including execution of any authorized renewals and any changes or amendments to the Agreement that do not exceed the amounts authorized herein.
